{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The number of spanning trees τ(G), weighted: the sum over spanning trees of the product of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"their weights, which is any cofactor of the Laplacian (Kirchhoff’s matrix-tree theorem)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Loops never lie on a tree; parallel edges each count. 0 for the empty graph and for a"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"disconnected one, 1 for one vertex.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"numberOfSpanningTrees","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Sd","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Double"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"BinaryFloatingPoint","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:SB"}],"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":": counts pass ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int"},{"text":" quickly (K₂₅ has 25²³). The Laplacian with one vertex removed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is eliminated densely as Grassmann, Taksar and Heyman eliminate (each pivot a sum of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"conductances, never a difference), so the count keeps a relative accuracy of about n · 10⁻¹⁶","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"whatever the weights; its pivots are multiplied with the binary exponent kept apart, so it","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"overflows only past ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"’s range, to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".infinity"},{"text":". When every weight is an integer","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"(unweighted included) and the count is below 2¹⁰⁰, it is computed exactly instead (two","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"determinants modulo 62-bit primes, combined by the Chinese remainder theorem) and rounded","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"once, so a count below 2⁵³ is exact. O(n³) time (less on sparse graphs), n² ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"text":"s.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"type":"text","text":" gives the weight of the edge at each position, read once per position; a weight of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"0 is no edge."}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every weight is finite and nonnegative."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside","style":"note","name":"Precondition"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/numberOfSpanningTrees(weight:)-28jjs"},"metadata":{"symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"name":"SpectralGraphTheory","relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"]}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ElectricalNetworks.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson